# The founder's example: a discount rule, kept values, records, and a list filtered with "where".

To calculate discount:
  Receive total and member
  When member is true and total is at least 100:
    Give 20% of total
  Otherwise:
    Give 0

Keep tax rate at 7%

An Order has:
  Item is text
  Price is money
  Paid is yes/no

Set orders to [an Order with item "pen" and price $1.50 and paid true, an Order with item "ink" and price $3.25 and paid false, an Order with item "pad" and price $2.10 and paid true]
Set total to the sum of prices from orders where paid is true
Set tax to round (total * tax rate) to 2 places
say "Paid orders come to {total}, plus {tax} tax."

say "A member spending 150 saves {calculate discount with 150 and true}."
say "A guest spending 150 saves {calculate discount with 150 and false}."

Test "members spending at least 100 get 20% off":
  Expect calculate discount with 150 and true to be 30
  Expect calculate discount with 100 and true to be 20

Test "no discount below 100 or for guests":
  Expect calculate discount with 99 and true to be 0
  Expect calculate discount with 150 and false to be 0
